    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d737">

                <pb facs="0792" n="688" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg688"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/2528</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Heath</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 228</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-10-04">October 4,
                        1932</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Department’s
                    telegram No. 66 of October 1, 3 p.m.,<anchor n="32" xml:id="d737-f1"/> there is
                    transmitted herewith the text of a note which you are instructed, unless you
                    perceive objection, to address to the Minister for Foreign Affairs in reply to
                    his note of September 26, 1932, forwarded with your despatch No. 503.<anchor
                        n="33" xml:id="d737-f2"/> If you have any comment in regard to this note, or
                    suggestion as to change in the text thereof, please cable promptly.</p>
                <p>You are authorized to agree to publication of the following: (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">a</hi>) your note of September 23; (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">b</hi>) the note of the Minister of Foreign Affairs
                    dated September 26; and (<hi rendition="#italic">c</hi>) the note which you are
                    now instructed to communicate to the Foreign Office. There appears to be no
                    reason for publication of the note you sent the Minister embodying the
                    Department’s telegram No. 63 of September 23, 5 p.m., regarding Haitianization
                    of the Department of the South, since this question is adequately covered in the
                    note you are now to communicate to him.</p>
                <p>Please advise by telegraph in advance of the date when the notes will be made
                    public in Haiti so that arrangements for simultaneous release may be made
                    here.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis White</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d737-a1.xml" xpointer="d737-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
